b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING incremental;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for assignment statements as replacement (4.2), arrays (5.2), recursive procedures and function designators with value parameters (4.7, 5.4), the for statement with a while element (4.6) and conditional statements (4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), atoms as integer codes and sequences as parallel arrays of heads and tail indices (systems file, Values), named quantities as variables, as batch 1C's P10a holds them (programs/algol-60/README.md), a program that reads each stage as it arrives, which counts as the same computation (systems file, The same computation), and the message loop and observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line k for every stage k: r p, what the stage brings, r being 1 for a request and 2 for a release, and p the code of the atom that makes it, A being 1 and B being 2;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P15d. holder and queue are named quantities, each one variable: holder an atom code, 0 for none, and queue a sequence. They start as none and the empty sequence. Each stage replaces them by its case, by assignment, the right sides taken at the values before the stage. p requests: if holder = none, holder becomes p, otherwise queue becomes queue ++ the sequence of p alone. p releases, where holder = p: if queue is empty, holder becomes none, otherwise, with queue = the sequence of h alone ++ t, holder becomes h and queue becomes t. A release by someone who is not the holder is not one the problem defines: the program reports no solution and leaves holder and queue as they were. A grant once made is not withdrawn: a later request only joins the queue. A sequence is a cell index into the arrays hd and tl, 0 being the empty sequence, and a cell c being the sequence of hd[c] alone ++ the sequence tl[c]. ++ makes a new sequence by the cases of conc, as in P03, copying its first place. The store of 10000 cells is fixed in one place;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, r, p, holder, queue, top, conc1, conc2, req1, req2, rel1, rel2;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ undefined;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ hd, tl[1:10000];

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ cons(h, t);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ h, t; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ h, t;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a new cell, the sequence of h alone ++ the sequence t;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ top := top + 1; hd[top] := h; tl[top] := t; cons := top e̲n̲d̲ cons;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ conc(a, b);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ a, b; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a, b;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a ++ b, by the cases of conc, in order. Case 1: conc(the empty sequence, b, b). Case 2: conc(the sequence of h alone ++ a, b, the sequence of h alone ++ c) if conc(a, b, c);
  i̲f̲ a = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ conc1 := conc1 + 1; conc := b e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ c;
    conc2 := conc2 + 1;
    c := conc(tl[a], b);
    conc := cons(hd[a], c)
  e̲n̲d̲ conc;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ num(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an integer, a minus sign if it is negative and then its decimal digits, with no spaces;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
    i̲f̲ v < 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`-'); num(-v) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ v ≥ 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ num(v ÷ 10);
      d := v - v ÷ 10 × 10;
      i̲f̲ d = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`0') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`1') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`2')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`3') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`4') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`5')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`6') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 7 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`7') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 8 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`8')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`9')
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ num;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ printseq(s);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ s; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ s;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a sequence of atom codes, in parentheses, separated by commas, with a new line after every ten;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j, c;
    PRINTTEXT(`(');
    c := 0;
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ s ≠ 0 d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      num(hd[s]); s := tl[s]; c := c + 1;
      i̲f̲ s ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      i̲f̲ c = 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ NLCR; c := 0 e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`)')
  e̲n̲d̲ printseq;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ printholder;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: the holder, as its atom code, or none;
  i̲f̲ holder = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`none') e̲l̲s̲e̲ num(holder);

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  top := conc1 := conc2 := req1 := req2 := rel1 := rel2 := 0;
  holder := 0; queue := 0;

  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲ d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: one message, and the stage it poses;
    code := read; k := read;
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the stage's constants: a request or a release, and who makes it;
    r := read; p := read;
    undefined := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
    i̲f̲ r = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ p requests;
      i̲f̲ holder = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ req1 := req1 + 1; holder := p e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ req2 := req2 + 1; queue := conc(queue, cons(p, 0)) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ r = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ p releases, where holder = p;
      i̲f̲ holder ≠ p t̲h̲e̲n̲ undefined := t̲r̲u̲e̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ queue = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ rel1 := rel1 + 1; holder := 0 e̲n̲d̲
      e̲l̲s̲e̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ rel2 := rel2 + 1; holder := hd[queue]; queue := tl[queue] e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ undefined := t̲r̲u̲e̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the answer: the values holder and queue have now;
    i̲f̲ ¬undefined t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      PRINTTEXT(`[answer]holder = '); printholder; PRINTTEXT(`, queue = '); printseq(queue); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the one value held for each named quantity, and how the waiting requests are held;
    PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
    i̲f̲ undefined t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution: a stage the problem does not define, holder and queue left as they were'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`atoms as codes: A is 1, B is 2, and none is 0'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`holder and queue are variables, replaced by assignment, and their earlier values are not kept'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`waiting requests: the atoms in queue, held as its elements, to be granted by a later release'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[bind holder]'); printholder; b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[bind queue]'); printseq(queue); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations request/1 '); num(req1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations request/2 '); num(req2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations release/1 '); num(rel1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations release/2 '); num(rel2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations conc/1 '); num(conc1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[operations conc/2 '); num(conc2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
